  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MERCI_Multisectoral Emergency Response for Conflict Impacted population in South</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This new project is a continuation of the DRCC07 project from the previous Humanitarian Programme Implementation Plan (PIP) (P00884) which closed on March 31, 2022. This project falls under the National Change Objectives (NCOS3). It is linked to the Oxfam International (OI) preparedness and response plan. Contributing to reduce the impact of humanitarian disasters on up to 740 000 affected people in eastern Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC) Provinces, this project will increase the effectiveness and timeliness of Oxfam&apos;s responses to humanitarian emergencies in DRC by establishment of an effectively managed and appropriate contingency stock, and setting up an Oxfam Emergency Response Team. Some key activities will be carried out, including the provision of safe drinking water through the construction of water points; the construction of sanitation facilities with hygiene promotion activities in the project areas; household livelihood support followed by education on the proper use of food. In addition, community protection activities will be carried out.  MERCI, une r&#xE9;ponse multisectorielle ax&#xE9;e sur la protection, vise &#xE0; r&#xE9;pondre aux besoins de 31 820 personnes (54% de femmes et de filles ; 19 701 enfants dont 14 813 &#xE2;g&#xE9;s de 5 &#xE0; 17 ans) touch&#xE9;es par les conflits interethniques dans dix communaut&#xE9;s de Bijombo (Bijombo centre, Muranvia, Kajembwe, Mugete, Irango, Mugogo), Katobo (Ndegu et Mashuba), Lemera et Bwegera. L&apos;objectif est d&apos;assurer une r&#xE9;ponse humanitaire ad&#xE9;quate, urgente et flexible pour servir les populations r&#xE9;cemment d&#xE9;plac&#xE9;es, les populations dans les zones de retour qui ont &#xE9;t&#xE9; partiellement ou compl&#xE8;tement d&#xE9;truites, et les communaut&#xE9;s h&#xF4;tes qui connaissent une vuln&#xE9;rabilit&#xE9; importante en raison du conflit et de la pression exerc&#xE9;e par les personnes d&#xE9;plac&#xE9;es sur leurs ressources limit&#xE9;es. Oxfam Belgique et ses partenaires posent que SI 1) les communaut&#xE9;s vuln&#xE9;rables dans le corridor Bijombo -Bwegera am&#xE9;liorent et &#xE9;tendent les structures de protection</narrative>
  </description>
